    _o75 = _r75.stdout.decode().strip()
    # retold v3.96 patch2: the CUDA build's field, and the Vulkan build's after it - checking, with no answer for it here
    check(_o75 == "~".join(_x75 + "|llama.cpp Vulkan|checking..." for _x75 in (
                   "llama.cpp CUDA|checking...|CUDA 12.4 - N/A|CUDA 13.3 - N/A|CUDA 13.4 - N/A", "llama.cpp CUDA|not installed|CUDA 12.4 - N/A|CUDA 13.3 - N/A|CUDA 13.4 - N/A",
                   "llama.cpp CUDA|CUDA 12.4 - N/A|CUDA 13.3 - b10628|Installed b10600|Update available!|CUDA 13.4 - N/A",
                   "llama.cpp CUDA|CUDA 12.4 - N/A|CUDA 13.3 - b10628|Installed b10628|CUDA 13.4 - N/A",
                   "llama.cpp CUDA|installed, but it will not say which build (commit 3f9ab12cd)|CUDA 12.4 - N/A|CUDA 13.3 - b10628|Installed commit 3f9ab12cd|CUDA 13.4 - N/A")),
          "run: the field says what is there and whether it is current, one row per line: a checking pill "
          "until it knows (patch13), a fault beside the name, the installed line carrying Installed and - when "
          "older - Update available!, and a build that cannot name itself named as it is (patch12)",
          _o75[:110] + _r75.stderr.decode()[:70])
