# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.76 patch93
section("v3.76 patch93: a report that can name its source")
# Three cards froze half read while the same logs parsed perfectly here, the
# door served them correctly under both a fresh and a stale watermark, and the
# tick's interval was proved to register. Everything measurable was right, which
# means the panel was reading a file nobody could see. So it says which.
# Separately, a real flaw in the patch88 settle rule: "ready" and the last
# buffers arrive in the SAME sweep of the log, so a report read a moment earlier
# can be both ready and short - and the rule stopped asking on it.
