# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.76 patch181
# Two field reports on p180. A Spark model scanned fine and its row said no
# family: the architecture string was in no table and under no prefix, so the
# label was blank while the card printed it. And spoken lines from one reply
# landed in the box of the reply before it: SkyrimNet sent the request twice,
# the dropped duplicate's stream escaped the write handler as a reset, its
# record was never written and its half-fed ledger entry stayed open for ever;
# and the placement rule preferred any reply whose cursor sat before the words,
# so a chunk voiced out of order was handed to the ghost that merely contained
# the same words. Now an unknown architecture is named from its own string,
# a dropped stream is recorded and its entry closed, and placement asks which
# reply contains the words - unspoken occurrences first, oldest reply first.
section("v3.76 patch181: every architecture has a name; a chunk goes to the reply that contains it")

