# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.80 patch65
# JEV Diagnostics says what is so, never what does nothing: llama-server hands a prompt to the GPU in
# calls of --batch-size tokens and the GPU computes each in micro-batches of --ubatch-size, so a pass
# larger than the batch costs nothing - patch64 warned it and told the owner to raise Batch size past
# 6000. Each line now is a calculation and a short fact; a warning is a real risk only.
