# The JEV view reads the server it describes: the decision type from that launch's own log, its figures cached by
# the log's launch header (slot logs are reused in rotation), and routes re-read when a card is saved. Kev's batch
# is its micro-batch - llama.cpp sets it so in embedding mode - and the panel says so where it matters.
section("v3.91 Beta: the JEV view reads its server; Kev's batch is its micro-batch")

