# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.91 patch3
# The TTS server can run on the CPU: Run on CPU starts audio.cpp on its CPU backend with every GPU
# hidden from it, greys the GPU and Clock Hold menus, and the field ends in the allocation line and
# resources box the Song Generator's has - both lines naming the card as the selectors do, its pin
# number, board partner and name, or the CPU by the name the system gives it. Folder Settings and
# Customization start level with the first nav entry. And a new main tab, Hub: LLM finds models on
# Hugging Face built on the bases SkyrimNet players run, by tag and kind, with each row's LM head,
# tie_word_embeddings and architecture read from its own config and tensor names, its model tree,
# and a card - the README as Hugging Face draws it, rebuilt from an allowlist - with a tensor check
# and the GGUFs to download; Decision Model is the decision downloader, moved from Server.
section("v3.91 patch3: TTS on the CPU; the audio allocation lines; Hub > LLM and Hub > Decision Model")

# --- Run on CPU, server side
