# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.91 patch7
# Tensor Parallelism, a server's own: -sm tensor is chosen when llama-server loads, so it belongs to the
# server card, above Draftless speculation - a switch, the GPUs to pool as switches with the server's own
# greyed as device 0, the shares --tensor-split takes, by memory bandwidth unless set. While it is on it
# holds what -sm tensor needs - Flash attention on, KV f16, Auto fit off, draft backend sampling off -
# greyed, and gives the owner's values back when it is off. A pooled GPU another server uses is allowed
# with a yellow warning; a build without -sm tensor, an architecture it does not work with or a pool of
# one refuses Start, and the fleet launcher skips a server the panel holds. Live Network draws the pool
# dashed. Every [--flag] on a card opens its own Sampler Guide entry - --ctx-checkpoints opened Context
# size. Run on CPU says whether the RAM can hold the chosen TTS and is greyed when it cannot. A download
# of several files is one bundle: its progress says "file n of N", it ends once with every file listed,
# and on Hub > LLM another quant of the running repo joins it.
section("v3.91 patch7: Tensor Parallelism per server; every card link opens its own guide entry; Run on CPU's RAM pre-check; a download of several files ends once")

