# ---------------------------------------------------------- v3.91 patch8
# Tensor Parallelism's shares are a number beside each pooled GPU, 1 when it joins, with the part of the model it
# gives that card; the slice-against-free-VRAM figures and their false warnings are gone, and the TTS and song
# servers count among what else runs on a card. A tensor-parallel server's allocator report is a window per GPU of
# its pool - a cut buffer by the card's share against the largest, exact on the largest, about elsewhere - with
# each card's total measured: the fleet launcher reads every card before the spawn, the panel again once it serves,
# and names what else loaded there. The KV cache a pool prints twice is counted once. Hub > LLM draws every row and
# asks only about the rows in view; both Hub lists have column lines; "+N" lists every GGUF repo of its kind; the
# model tree shows names whole, scrolls sideways and its elbows meet; the Decision page's llama.cpp label is a way
# to its Backend Engines page; Hub rows wear the server cards' fold arrow.
section("v3.91 patch8: Tensor Parallelism's share per GPU and its allocator report per card, measured; Hub > LLM draws every row and reads the rows in view; column lines; +N's list; the model tree's names whole")

